From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@smartrg.com>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 06:58:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: xt_FLOWOFFLOAD: do not offload multicast

A flow holds one output per direction, which it resolves when it is
added. The outputs of a multicast route change when listeners join
or leave. So a multicast flow in the flowtable continues to send to
the output that it resolved, also after the last listener left, and
the counters of the multicast routing stop.

xt_flowoffload_route() sets no source address for the reverse route
lookup of IPv4, so the lookup succeeds for a multicast flow. IPv4
multicast that ipmr forwards and IPv6 multicast that ip6mr forwards
both go into the flowtable.

Skip a multicast destination for both families.
---
 net/netfilter/xt_FLOWOFFLOAD.c |   11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/xt_FLOWOFFLOAD.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/xt_FLOWOFFLOAD.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <linux/netfilter/xt_FLOWOFFLOAD.h>
 #include <linux/if_vlan.h>
 #include <net/ip.h>
+#include <net/ipv6.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_extend.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_helper.h>
@@ -250,6 +251,16 @@ xt_flowoffload_skip(struct sk_buff *skb,
 			return true;
 	}
 
+	/* A flow keeps the output it resolved at offload time, but the
+	 * outputs of a multicast route change when listeners join or leave.
+	 */
+	switch (family) {
+	case NFPROTO_IPV4:
+		return ipv4_is_multicast(ip_hdr(skb)->daddr);
+	case NFPROTO_IPV6:
+		return ipv6_addr_is_multicast(&ipv6_hdr(skb)->daddr);
+	}
+
 	return false;
 }
 
